              <p>
                For example, if a private vehicle costs a fixed amount for a round trip, two travelers would divide that total by two, while four travelers would divide it by four. The vehicle price itself does not necessarily change simply because the group has more passengers, provided the vehicle remains suitable for the group and luggage. This is why private transportation can become more cost-efficient on a per-person basis as group size increases.
              </p>

